---
import Layout from '../../../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import '../../../../styles/equipment.css';
import {defaults,limits} from '../../../../../public/equipment/14-10/solver.mjs';
const base='/equipment/14-10/';
const labels={radiusMm:'Mandrel surface radius (mm)',couponThicknessUm:'Substrate thickness (µm)',lengthMm:'Trace length (mm)',widthMm:'Trace width (mm)',sheetOhm:'Baseline sheet resistance (Ω/□)',cycles:'Schedule length (cycles)',frequencyHz:'Schedule frequency (Hz)',referenceLife:'Synthetic life at 1% strain (cycles)',exponent:'Synthetic strain exponent',driftAtLimit:'Synthetic fractional drift at damage 1',injectedOpen:'Inject open cycle (0 disables)'};
---
<Layout pageTitle="Cyclic bend fixture · trace fatigue" description="Resume a flexible trace test and discover a deliberately injected open circuit using a virtual motorized mandrel fixture." wide={true}>
<article class="equipment fx">
<nav class="eq-nav"><a href="/simulations/equipment/14-10/">← Equipment 14-10</a><a href="/simulations/equipment/">Equipment register</a><a href="#fx-reference">References & verification</a></nav>
<header class="eq-mast"><span class="eq-meta">14-10 · FLEXURAL TESTING / FIRST PASS</span><h2>Motorized cyclic bend fixture</h2><p>Wrap an inert flexible conductor around a mandrel, monitor its resistance, and catch an open circuit. Start the default 120-cycle exercise, or stop at 60 and save a checkpoint to compare the two paths.</p></header>
<div class="grid"><section><h3>Fixture</h3><div id="fx-view" aria-label="Orbitable metric model of motor, mandrel, grips and continuity controller"></div><div class="bar"><button data-fx-view="overall">Reset view</button><button data-fx-view="detail">Mandrel and grips</button><button data-fx-view="rear">Rear</button></div><p id="fx-ready" role="status">Loading metric model…</p><p>Drag to orbit; scroll or pinch to zoom. Click the turquoise jog button or use the matching control to move the sample between flat and 90°.</p></section>
<section><h3>Inert trace and schedule</h3><div class="fields">
{Object.entries(defaults).map(([key,value])=><label>{labels[key]}<input id={'fx-'+key} type="number" min={limits[key][0]} max={limits[key][1]} step={['injectedOpen','referenceLife','cycles'].includes(key)?'1':'any'} value={value}/></label>)}</div>
<div class="bar"><button id="fx-load">Unload coupon</button><button id="fx-jog">Jog to 90°</button><button id="fx-run" class="primary">Run remaining cycles</button><button id="fx-pause">Run to cycle 60</button><button id="fx-reset">Clear run</button></div>
<p id="fx-status" aria-live="polite">Default inert coupon loaded; the first open is intentionally injected at cycle 100. Cycles are computed in a batch, not at physical speed.</p></section></div>
<section><h3>Continuity history</h3><div class="grid"><canvas id="fx-chart" width="700" height="270" aria-label="End-of-cycle resistance chart with an open circuit event marker"></canvas><div><output id="fx-result">No cycles acquired.</output><div class="bar"><button id="fx-checkpoint" disabled>Save checkpoint</button><button id="fx-json" disabled>History JSON</button><button id="fx-csv" disabled>History CSV</button></div><label>Restore checkpoint (JSON)<input id="fx-restore" type="file" accept="application/json,.json"/></label></div></div></section>
<section id="fx-reference"><h3>Geometry and experimental model</h3>
<p>This is an <strong>original, unbuilt BTS fixture</strong>, not a manufacturer replica. All hardware dimensions are nominal design values, not measurements. The motor rotates the bend arm from flat to 90° and back. The load sensor is geometry only; the first-pass calculation does not predict force, grip slip or dynamics.</p>
<figure><img src={base+'reference.svg'} width="850" height="270" loading="lazy" alt="Annotated plan showing the motor axis, mandrel, fixed and moving grips, sensor location, and two continuity leads"/><figcaption>Original concept diagram, BTS 14-10 design r1 (not a photograph). <a href="https://engineering.case.edu/sites/default/files/styles/large/public/flex_tester_new_small.png?itok=Ip7IMbwy">Case Western Reserve University fixture photo</a> shows an external motorized flex-meter reference; no replica dimensions were taken from it.</figcaption></figure>
<p>The coupon is an ideal substrate with a negligibly thin, straight conductive trace at its outer surface. At full wrap, the neutral radius is <code>Rₙ = Rₘ + t/2</code>, peak curvature is <code>1/Rₙ</code> and tensile strain is <code>t/(2Rₙ)</code> (compare <a href="https://doi.org/10.3390/ma12152490">Kim et al., Eq. 1 and Fig. 1</a>). Resistance is sampled once back at flat, so the example excludes reversible gauge strain. The baseline is <code>R₀ = R□ L/w</code>; the cumulative teaching law is <code>D(N) = N/N₁% · (ε/0.01)^m</code> and flat resistance <code>R₀(1 + aD)</code> until damage reaches 1 or the injected open occurs. Open values are null in JSON and blank in CSV. The first event is kept once, even if further model cycles are recorded.</p>
<p>The two-terminal continuity idea follows the workflow illustrated in <a href="https://www.ipc.org/sites/default/files/test_methods_docs/2.4.3.1c.pdf">IPC-TM-650 2.4.3.1C</a> and the <a href="https://engineering.case.edu/research/centers/ammrc/fatigue_ductility_flex_tester">Case School facility page</a>, not a standards-compliance claim. All fatigue constants are editable synthetic calibration parameters, not measured material properties. There is no fitted lifetime curve, contact resistance, noise, fatigue validation, composite neutral-axis shift, or experimental data replay.</p>
<div class="scroll"><table><thead><tr><th>Check or specification</th><th>Expected / nominal</th><th>Actual and interpretation</th></tr></thead><tbody>
<tr><td>Baseplate W × D × T</td><td>320 × 220 × 18 mm</td><td>320 × 220 × 18 mm nominal original GLB geometry; no measured instrument.</td></tr>
<tr><td>Model test envelope</td><td>2–15 mm mandrel radius; 0.1–5 Hz schedule; ≤3% modeled strain</td><td>Arc must fit inside trace length. These are teaching bounds, not equipment ratings.</td></tr>
<tr><td>Neutral curvature and crest strain</td><td>200 m⁻¹; 1%</td><td>200 m⁻¹; 1%, absolute tolerances 10⁻⁹ m⁻¹ and 10⁻¹² strain fraction.</td></tr>
<tr><td>20-square trace; last closed sample</td><td>10 Ω initially; 10.495 Ω at cycle 99</td><td>10 Ω; 10.495 Ω, within 10⁻¹² Ω analytical tolerance.</td></tr>
<tr><td>Resume at cycle 60; inject open at cycle 100</td><td>Identical rows; exactly one event at 100</td><td>Exact match; all later resistance samples remain null.</td></tr>
</tbody></table></div>
<p><a href={base+'model.py'} download>Editable Blender generator</a> · <a href={base+'cyclic-bend.glb'} download>Metric GLB</a> · <a href={base+'xr-manifest.json'}>VR action contract</a> · <a href={base+'verification.json'}>Verification</a> · <a href={base+'reference-cases.json'}>Reference cases</a> · <a href={base+'example-checkpoint.json'} download>Example checkpoint</a> · <a href={base+'example-history.json'}>Output format example</a></p>
<p>Metric geometry and the shared jog action are suitable for later XR integration, but this page is not a headset session. No compatible downstream instrument reader is claimed.</p></section>
</article></Layout>
<script>import '../../../../lib/equipment/14-10/browser.mjs';</script>
<style>
.fx{max-width:76rem}.fx .grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(2,minmax(0,1fr));gap:1rem}.fx section{border-top:1px solid var(--border);padding:.8rem 0;margin:.8rem 0;min-width:0}.fx #fx-view{height:clamp(270px,31vw,420px);background:#d7dddf;touch-action:none}.fx #fx-view :global(canvas){display:block;width:100%;height:100%}.fx .bar{display:flex;gap:.42rem;flex-wrap:wrap;margin:.65rem 0}.fx .fields{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(2,minmax(0,1fr));gap:.48rem}.fx label{display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:.18em;font-size:.92rem}.fx input,.fx button{font:inherit;min-width:0;max-width:100%;min-height:2.4em;border:1px solid var(--border);border-radius:.16rem;padding:.36em .54em;background:var(--panel);color:var(--text)}.fx button{cursor:pointer}.fx button:disabled{opacity:.52;cursor:default}.fx .primary{color:white;background:#22534f}.fx #fx-status.error{color:#a64b31}.fx #fx-result{display:block;white-space:pre-line;font-family:monospace}.fx #fx-chart,.fx figure img{width:100%;height:auto}.fx figure{margin:1rem 0}.fx table{border-collapse:collapse;font-size:.88rem}.fx th,.fx td{border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);padding:.44rem;text-align:left}.fx .scroll{overflow:auto}@media(max-width:790px){.fx .grid{grid-template-columns:1fr}}
</style>
